<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Cataphract (VFEP v3.09, commit 31cee5e,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml); fields not discussed here are the
    Cataphract's. Tier, research, tags and the art follow the armor's header.

    - ToxicEnvironmentResistance +0.15, the shoulders' share of the set's 1.1 (rationale in the
      armor's header).
    - Costs: Comp 2 is the gas jet's nozzle (VFEP's Controller shoulders likewise pay components
      for their verb); Steel 55 and Plasteel 20 put the piece in the 7th-gen band.

    Gas jet: an apparel verb (ToxinWarcasket.Verb_SprayGas), as the Barrage shoulders carry
    theirs, so this piece redeclares tickerType Normal for the verb tracker and the AI check (the
    shoulder base leaves it at Never). A jet is two thirds of a tox pack, shaped: 10 tank charges
    at the armor's 3 cells each are 30 cells against the pack's 45, spread evenly over the cells
    the cone reaches. A 12 degree half-angle cone from 3 cells out to 12.9 is about 32 cells, so
    an open cone lands just under full density; walls shrink the cone and concentrate it, and
    past a full cell GasGrid.AddGas thickens the edges with the excess. coneStart 3: the angle
    test makes the cone a single-cell line for its first four cells, the pilot is immune and
    whoever stands beside them is not, and a one-wide stem bleeds sideways as much as any edge,
    so the shot begins where the cone is already three wide. The gas then spreads past the cone
    as the grid equalizes neighbours down to a step of 34, so the targeter draws two areas: the
    cone the gas lands in, and around it the cells expected to hold spreadMinGas or more within
    spreadTicks of the shot, from GasSpreadEstimate's replay of the grid's own rules. The
    threshold is 1, any gas at all, because that is what the player sees: SectionLayer_Gas hands
    each cell's raw density to the vertex colour, which clamps to 1, so a cell holding one unit
    draws exactly like a full one and the cloud shows no dose. The outer area is therefore where
    the cloud will show, and the cone itself is the part that bites: the first ring gets half the
    cone's density on the grid's first push, the next a quarter, the third a trace. At the
    defaults that is about 133 cells, four times the cone, three rings deep and back to the
    pilot's neighbours, which is the cloud a shot leaves on open ground. halfAngle and range are
    the defaults of their mod settings. Warmup 1 s.
    - Fuel (ToxinWarcasket.CompJetNozzle): 10 charges from the armor's tank when it holds them,
      otherwise one of the nozzle's two reserve jets, each reloaded with those charges' 20
      chemfuel; two so the shoulders are worth wearing alone. tankChargesPerShot and maxCharges
      are the defaults of their mod settings (the jet's cost and reserve), and the settings
      recompute ammoCountPerCharge as the cost times the armor's chemfuel per charge, so the 20
      here is only the default's product. The command's corner counts jets left, the tank's and
      the reserves' together, so a full tank and loaded reserves read 6 / 6; alone, the reserves'
      2 / 2. Its tooltip is jetDescription, as the gear's own description is the set's lore.
    - onlyManualCast, as the Barrage's: a drafted colonist never fires it on its own. Raiders
      fire it through the nozzle's own check, at the densest group of hostile humanlikes the gas
      would affect, never into their own faction's.

    Compat: SOS2Patch.xml leaves shoulder pads alone, as VFEP's own patch does for VFEP's.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase">
    <defName>TXWC_WarcasketShoulders_Toxin</defName>
    <label>toxin warcasket shoulders</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized warcasket pauldrons with superior protection and worse weight, fitted with shoulder-mounted nozzles that spray tox gas from the shell's tank.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized warcasket pauldrons with superior protection and worse weight, fitted with shoulder-mounted nozzles that spray tox gas from the shell's tank.\n\nThe 7th generation warcaskets came after underwhelming results in improving the baseline performance even further, instead focusing on creating designs that, while interchangeable, work better as a set. They were also the first to include plasteel in the design as it appeared more frequently in scavenging and looting. Each piece has a unique function that synergises with those of the same series, making them a truly separate class of mobile armor units.\n\nThe Toxin series rebuilt the old Cataphract chassis for chemical warfare. A gas tank in the shell feeds both the vents around the pilot and the nozzles on the pauldrons, and the helmet's respirator filters the air and draws spent gas back into the tank, so a pilot can flood a position, breathe it unharmed and reclaim the cloud once the work is done. A toxin pilot rarely falls alone: the tank bursts where they lie. Their motto, muffled through the respirator, is to breathe easy.</description>
    <tickerType>Normal</tickerType>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketToxin/WarcasketToxinShoulders</texPath>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>35</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>1.56</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.65</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>0.78</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>18</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>6</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MoveSpeed>-0.35</MoveSpeed>
      <ToxicEnvironmentResistance>0.15</ToxicEnvironmentResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.2</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentIndustrial>2</ComponentIndustrial>
      <Steel>55</Steel>
      <Plasteel>20</Plasteel>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpecialisedWarcaskets</li>
      <li>ToxGas</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Shoulders</li>
        <li>Arms</li>
        <li>Hands</li>
        <li>Neck</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketToxin/WarcasketToxinShoulders</wornGraphicPath>
      <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketSpecialised</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="ToxinWarcasket.CompProperties_JetNozzle">
        <maxCharges>2</maxCharges>
        <chargeNoun>jet</chargeNoun>
        <ammoDef>Chemfuel</ammoDef>
        <ammoCountPerCharge>20</ammoCountPerCharge>
        <baseReloadTicks>60</baseReloadTicks>
        <soundReload>Standard_Reload</soundReload>
        <hotKey>Misc4</hotKey>
        <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
        <tankChargesPerShot>10</tankChargesPerShot>
        <jetDescription>Spray a cone of tox gas from the shoulder nozzles toward the target. The gas lands in the inner cone and drifts over the outer area, thinning as it goes. Each jet draws on the warcasket's tank while it holds enough, and otherwise spends one of the nozzles' own reserve jets, which are reloaded with chemfuel.</jetDescription>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <verbs>
      <li Class="ToxinWarcasket.VerbProperties_SprayGas">
        <label>gas jet</label>
        <hasStandardCommand>true</hasStandardCommand>
        <onlyManualCast>true</onlyManualCast>
        <range>12.9</range>
        <warmupTime>1</warmupTime>
        <noiseRadius>4</noiseRadius>
        <commandIcon>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/ToxPack/ToxPack</commandIcon>
        <soundCast>GasPack_Deploy</soundCast>
        <targetParams>
          <canTargetLocations>true</canTargetLocations>
        </targetParams>
        <halfAngle>12</halfAngle>
        <coneStart>3</coneStart>
        <propagationSpeed>0.6</propagationSpeed>
        <spreadMinGas>1</spreadMinGas>
        <spreadTicks>300</spreadTicks>
        <sprayEffecter>TXWC_GasJetSpray</sprayEffecter>
        <sprayEffecterTicks>14</sprayEffecterTicks>
      </li>
    </verbs>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
